Copy mode: copy a frame as soon as its GPU work is done instead of at the next vsync tick.
The vsync tick copied a pending frame only if the GPU work submitted before its swap had completed (0229); otherwise the
frame waited for the next tick, and by then CoreAnimation had mostly swapped the next frame, which replaced it. A home
swipe on beryllium (boot 40, kern.sweet_fb_trace) lost 35 of 125 frames that way while the GPU was ~80 % idle: backboardd
submitted a frame every ~22 ms (median), the panel got ~70 % of them. Now such a tick arms a timer (copy mode only; direct
mode has its own swap timer) that checks the gate every 250 us and copies the frame the moment it opens. present() draws
into the back buffer and flips at the next latch exactly as at a tick, so there is no tearing. The 250-us checks are not
counted in gpu_holds; a 50 ms wait still ends the hold as before. New in kern.sweet_fb: copyasap=, gate_copies= (frames
copied this way). Writable sysctl kern.sweet_fb_copyasap (default 1; 0 = the old behaviour, for comparing in one boot);
boot-arg sweetfb_copyasap sets the initial value.

